<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jan Smuts</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1870–1950</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jan Smuts was a South African statesman who fought as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> general and then, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-botha">Louis Botha</a>, led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/het-volk">Het Volk</a> party in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transvaal">Transvaal</a> Colony and negotiated union in 1910. He was prime minister of the Union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> in 1919–1924 and 1939–1948, served in the British war cabinets and helped found the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-nations">League of Nations</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jan-smuts.jpg" alt="Jan Smuts" width="320" height="452" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown - Toesprake deur sy hoog-edeagbare JC Smuts · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Genl_JC_Smuts.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
